<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 18 March, from 1229 to 2014.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jerusalem.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1229 CE <span class="tih-ago">797 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Frederick II crowns himself King of Jerusalem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Having regained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> by treaty while excommunicated, the Emperor took the crown from the altar of the Holy Sepulchre and placed it on his own head. No cleric would crown him.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1848 CE <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Street fighting erupts in Berlin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Troops fired on a crowd outside the royal palace and barricade fighting spread through the city, leaving hundreds dead. King Frederick William IV withdrew the army and promised a constitution.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1871 CE <span class="tih-ago">155 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Parisians rise up and begin the Paris Commune</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Attempts by the government to remove the National Guard's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montmartre">Montmartre</a> provoked an uprising. The Commune ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> until it was crushed in the 'Bloody Week' of May.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1965 CE <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexei Leonov makes the first spacewalk</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soviet cosmonaut spent about 12 minutes outside Voskhod 2. His suit ballooned in the vacuum, and he had to let out air to squeeze back into the airlock.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1990 CE <span class="tih-ago">36 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">East Germany holds its first free elections</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">East Germans voted in their first free parliamentary elections. The conservative Alliance for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> won, opening the way to rapid reunification with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a> in October.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2014 CE <span class="tih-ago">12 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Russia signs a treaty annexing Crimea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two days after a referendum held under Russian military control, Vladimir Putin signed a treaty absorbing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>. Most UN members regard the annexation as illegal.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a></div></div></li></ol>
